# HakiOS fragment: the Redmi Note 11T Pro (xaga) -- what is true of this phone and of no other with an MT6895.
#
# The panel is 1080 x 2460 ("panel-l16-42-02-0a-dsc-vdo", Tianma, DSC video mode), and mtkloader hands the
# kernel that size in boot_args (mtk/mt6895/loader/board.h: PANEL_W/PANEL_H). The iPhone picture is drawn at
# 750 x 1624 (fbscale=2, the iPhone X's 375 x 812 points at two pixels a point) and then scaled to the panel's
# width -- 1080/750 is 1.44 -- which is 2338 rows of the 2460, leaving 61 rows of black above and below
# (fbfit=1, "keeps its proportions"). fbfit=3, what x6826b uses, is wrong here: it draws one pixel to one
# pixel, and 750 x 1624 in the middle of a 1080 x 2460 panel is a small picture, not a full one.
#
# fbfit is 0: the picture is the panel. boot_args names the panel 1080 x 2460 and the kernel now
# draws an identity picture of exactly that size ("picture 1080x2460 crop 0 fill 1080" in the log),
# so there is no scaling left to describe. It matters beyond looks: hakios.nvt.c's picture_y()
# reads the same fbfit and used to squash the panel's 2460 rows into PICTURE_H_ON_W = 1080 * 2436 /
# 1125 = 2338 and drop them by PICTURE_TOP = 61, while the picture on screen was already one row to
# one row -- so a finger at the bottom of the panel was reported sixty-one rows high and about five
# per cent short, and the further down the worse it got. With fbfit=0 both sides are identity.
#
# fb_flip is left off on purpose. It points OVL0 at a second picture, and its two addresses (FLIP_OVL0
# 0x1400b000, FLIP_LK_FB_BASE 0x787b0000) are the MT6768's, compiled into MiniIOMobileFramebuffer.cpp; on this
# SoC the overlay is at 0x14002000 and LK's framebuffer at 0xfe14e000, so the flip would fail its own bounds
# check and log "not flipping" -- harmless, but there is nothing to gain from asking.
#
# The touch screen and the buttons go through CONFIG_BOOTARGS rather than CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN, because
# CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN is one switch that can only say "the phone's touch screen" -- it becomes
# touchscreen=1, redwood's numbering. This phone has two parts of its own, and each driver asks for
# its own number: the Novatek NT36672E takes touchscreen=3, the keypad and the MT6363 take buttons=2
# (mtk/mt6895/drivers/input/hakios.nvt.c and hakios.mt6895_keys.c). keylog=2 is on for the first boots:
# the keypad's register layout is not in any source here, so the driver prints the block every second
# until the offsets in hakios.mt6895_keys.c can be pinned down; drop it once they are.
CONFIG_DEVICE="xaga"
CONFIG_FBSCALE=2
# fbfit=0: one panel pixel to one picture pixel. fbfit=1 kept the 1125x2436 picture's proportions
# inside 1080x2460, which squeezed it into 2338 rows and pushed it down 61; that was right while the
# picture itself was a different shape from the panel, but the framebuffer now reports 1080x2460
# with crop 0 and fill 1080 (see the fb_disp dump), so the picture already covers the panel and the
# extra twenty-three-hundredths scale only made every touch land off its target.
CONFIG_FBFIT=0
CONFIG_FB_QUEUE=1
CONFIG_FB_INUSE=y
CONFIG_BOOTARGS="buttons=2 touchscreen=3 keylog=1 key_scan=1 fbwidth=1080 fbheight=2460 fb_disp=1 mali=6 mali_cold=0 mali_preas0=1 headset=1"
